          "title": "PostmarketOS is rebranding as Nura",
          "url": "https://nura.eco/blog/2026/09/27/nura-rename/",
          "source": "Hacker News",
          "date": "2026-09-27T15:31:15Z",
          "language": "en",
          "section": "us_news",
          "raw_content": "After a one and a half year selection process , the new name of the operating system formerly known postmarketOS has been announced during the mystery talk of our very own conference. From now on this project is known as Nura! Nuraghe from Macomer by Sailko , CC-BY-3.0 Nura comes as an abbreviation of Nuraghe , which are ancient (3000 BC and older) granite structures found in Sardinia in Italy, many of which still stand today. The deeper meaning is the stability and the resistance to millenniums, which fits well with the our project as the idea has been from the start to keep devices our OS runs on useful for a long time. The name was contributed by Davide Depau as part of our initial request for community contributions for the new name. Thanks a lot Davide! FAQ Why are you renaming the project? Through the years, most members of the team have experienced difficulties doing outreach for ",
